From: Claude (CT108) <claude@ct108>
Subject: soc: qcom: icc-bwmon / PCI: qcom: drop DDR votes in s2idle (X1E80100 EL2)

Tracing icc_set_bw across s2idle on a Surface Pro 11 at EL2 showed DDR LPM never entered because two votes stayed
on ebi: the CPU bwmon (24091000.pmu, 800 MB/s peak, no PM ops) and pcie-qcom's 1 kBps "keep data path" vote.
bwmon: add suspend/resume that stops the monitor and drops the OPP vote. pcie-qcom: vote 0 in suspend-to-idle.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/icc-bwmon.c
Update 17-10: the zero PCIe vote hung the SoC entering s2idle at EL2, so it is opt-in (pcie_qcom.s2idle_zero_vote).

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -1682,8 +1682,14 @@
 	width = FIELD_GET(PCI_EXP_LNKSTA_NLW, status);
 
 	if (pcie->icc_mem) {
-		ret = icc_set_bw(pcie->icc_mem, 0,
-				 width * QCOM_PCIE_LINK_SPEED_TO_BW(speed));
+		/*
+		 * Don't vote the full link bandwidth: as peak or as average it
+		 * pins DDR at 2092 MHz for as long as the link is up, even when
+		 * it idles in L1ss (AOP DDR stats, 2026-10-01). Keep the boot-time
+		 * Gen1 x1 vote; real DMA traffic is seen by the LLCC->DDR BWMON,
+		 * which scales DDR up.
+		 */
+		ret = icc_set_bw(pcie->icc_mem, 0, QCOM_PCIE_LINK_SPEED_TO_BW(1));
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(pci->dev, "Failed to set bandwidth for PCIe-MEM interconnect path: %d\n",
 				ret);
@@ -2193,6 +2199,10 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/* EL2 experiment: zero PCIe-MEM vote in s2idle; the first try hung the SoC on suspend, so it is opt-in */
+static bool s2idle_zero_vote;
+module_param(s2idle_zero_vote, bool, 0644);
+
 static int qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_pcie *pcie;
@@ -2223,7 +2233,14 @@
 		 * functional during suspend.
 		 */
 		if (pcie->icc_mem) {
-			ret = icc_set_bw(pcie->icc_mem, 0, kBps_to_icc(1));
+			/*
+			 * Any non-zero vote keeps DDR out of self-refresh; in s2idle nothing
+			 * moves data, so let the path drop to zero (X1E80100: DDR LPM was
+			 * never entered with the 1 kBps vote left by this driver).
+			 */
+			ret = icc_set_bw(pcie->icc_mem, 0,
+					 (s2idle_zero_vote && pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE) ?
+					 0 : kBps_to_icc(1));
 			if (ret) {
 				dev_err(dev,
 					"Failed to set bandwidth for PCIe-MEM interconnect path: %d\n",
